  "key_1487728205": "Remember:",
  "key_688195319986046893": " Ready to play golf ?",
  "key_638882354": "Choose a Beastie to join you",
  "key_3022171554645389797": "Congratulations!",
  "key_1166333281": "Drag anywhere to aim\n\nRelease to swing!",
  "key_1076606632": "Look at the target number",
  "key_1392070223": "Choose the hole with the equivalent value!",
  "key_1482019100": "Every digit in a number has a place value.\nThis means its position tells us how much it is worth.",
  "key_925070597": " place value\n",
  "key_1098797788": "Digits to the left of the decimal point are whole numbers, and digits to the right are decimals.",
  "key_1394757685": "decimal point",
  "key_1604119244": "decimals",
  "key_1596733328": "Today we will focus on decimal parts.\nThey represent values smaller than one.",
  "key_463141685": "decimal parts",
  "key_1030798127": "Here we have 5 tenths of a whole.",
  "key_1576573258": "Next, 9 hundredths of a whole number.",
  "key_2132556311": "And here, 7 thousandths of a whole.",
  "key_2022921664": "Use the place value names \nto aim for the right hole!",
  "key_1109674376": "5 Tenths = 0.5",
  "key_34867809": "9 Hundredths = 0.09",
  "key_1972261066": "7 Thousandths = 0.007",
  "key_2040290034": "Six and Seven Tenths",
  "key_1916941575": "Six and Seven Hundredths",
  "key_413638833": "Start by reading as you normally would.",
  "key_483924095": "Next, when we reach the decimal point, we always say “and.”",
  "key_2049422137": "Then, read the decimal part like a whole number and add the place value of the last digit.",
  "key_784906587": "decimal part",
  "key_1985527660": "Reading it all together, we get:\r",
  "key_2109683873": "Remeber: \n\nThe name at the end depends on the place value of the last digit in the decimal part.\r",
  "key_844712919": "  Three hundred ",
  "key_138851529": "seven ",
  "key_163801395": "tenths",
  "key_640949874": "and",
  "key_625248270": "Five",
  "key_25549760": "eight",
  "key_1673532693": "hundredths",
  "key_898383866": "Four hundred eighty-two",
  "key_1721529431": "Six hundred ninety-five thousandths",
  "key_2078987490": "thousandths",
  "key_1079416684": "2 hundreds is the same as multiplying 2 by 100.",
  "key_1971493391": "8 tens is the same as multiplying 8 by 10",
  "key_1503700232": "And 5 ones is the same as multiplying 5 by 1",
  "key_178080841": "Next, the 6 in the tenths place means 6 divided by 10.",
  "key_2080893306": "The 7 in the hundredths place means 7 divided by 100.",
  "key_640664925": "And the 4 in the thousandths place represents 4 divided by 1000.",
  "key_399447526": "That’s our number in expanded form!",
  "key_112144178": "Remember, it can also be written like this:",
  "key_1653570498": "Nice work! Let’s use expanded form to hit the right holes!",
  "key_1799175421": "Remember:\n\nCompare numbers by using place value and breaking them into expanded form.",
  "key_1088487279": " expanded form.",
